@startuml sequence-policy-replacement
!include style.iuml
title Replace hardcoded policies (a rule change is a new policy)

actor "Authority\n(account 0)" as Authority
actor "Holder" as Holder
participant "ChoreographyNMT" as NMT
participant "MasterSmartPolicy" as Master
participant "MasterSmartPolicyFrozen" as Frozen
participant "ChoreographyMutableAsset" as Asset
participant "CreatorSmartPolicy" as Creator
participant "CreatorSmartPolicyPaperScenario" as Paper

== Freeze transfers and versions ==
Authority -> Frozen ** : deploy
Authority -> NMT : setMasterSmartPolicy(frozen)
NMT -> Master : evaluate(authority, action, nmt)
Master --> NMT : subject == administrator
NMT -> NMT : masterSmartPolicy = frozen,\nemit MasterSmartPolicyChanged
Holder -> NMT : transferFrom(holder, partner, tokenId)
NMT -> Frozen : evaluate(holder, action, asset)
Frozen --> NMT : false
NMT --> Holder : revert MasterDenied()

== Install BPMN constraints on an asset ==
Authority -> Paper ** : deploy(participantAM)
Authority -> Asset : setCreatorSmartPolicy(paper)
Asset -> Creator : evaluate(authority, msg.data, asset)
Creator --> Asset : subject == administrator
Asset -> Asset : creatorSmartPolicy = paper
Holder -> Asset : setCreatorSmartPolicy(other)
Asset -> Paper : evaluate(holder, msg.data, asset)
Paper --> Asset : false
Asset --> Holder : revert OperationDenied(0)

note over Master, Paper
  No policy has runtime setters: rules are literals,
  as in a policy translated from XACML. Each policy
  is replaced only with the approval of the current one.
end note
@enduml
